flowchart TB
    accTitle: The code of the hooks
    accDescr: MkDocs, the scripts and the workflows run .github/mkdocs_project.py, which passes on what they ask for to the modules of .github/hub/. Each module imports only those below it. The event hooks of MkDocs use the files of the address and what a project works with, which use the releases, the search and the cards. The catalog bot uses what a project works with and the cards. The check of the built website and the watch of the live websites use the files of the address and what they read of a website. Everything rests on the reader, the web and the catalog.

    run(["MkDocs, the scripts<br>and the workflows"])
    entry["mkdocs_<br>project.py<br>the event hooks and the options"]
    events["events.py<br>the event hooks of MkDocs"]
    check["sitecheck.py<br>the check of the built website"]
    bot["bot.py<br>the catalog bot and its fix"]
    watch["watch.py<br>the watch of the live websites"]
    pictures["pictures.py<br>the pictures of the cards"]
    address["address.py<br>the files at the root, the old pages"]
    requirements["requirements<br>.py<br>what a project works with"]
    built["built.py<br>what they read of a website"]
    releases["releases.py<br>What's new and the Releases page"]
    render["render.py<br>the cards, the Trust page, the tables"]
    search["search.py<br>the search of every project"]
    reader["reader.py<br>reads projects.toml"]
    web["web.py<br>asks the web"]
    catalog["catalog.py<br>the projects as data"]

    run --> entry
    entry --> events & check & bot & watch & pictures
    events --> address & requirements
    check & watch --> address & built
    bot --> requirements & render
    pictures --> web
    address & requirements --> releases
    address --> search
    releases --> render & search
    search --> reader
    render & search & reader --> catalog
    render & search --> web
    web --> catalog

